<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The application's identity: the two colours of the mark itself, the green
    it is laid on and the white it is drawn in.

    They stay separate from the theme's tokens on purpose. Those tokens dress
    the interface and follow the light or dark theme, whereas the mark has one
    appearance: the launcher draws the icon long before the application starts,
    and the opening screen (SPEC §7.0) shows that same icon, so neither may
    follow anything. Pointing these at @color/signal and @color/surface would
    repaint the icon and lighten the opening the day the dark theme is picked
    up, and the white bicycle would then sit on a pale green.

    The ground holds the same value as `signal` in the light theme, and the ink
    the same as `surface`. Changing the identity's green therefore means
    changing this file and the light theme together.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="identity_ground">#0F6E56</color>
    <color name="identity_ink">#F9FCFA</color>
</resources>
